Based on the following JSON specification for the 'SmartHome-Nexus v2.1' API, generate a comprehensive technical documentation page. The documentation must include: 1) A 'Getting Started' section with a Python code example using the 'requests' library to authenticate. 2) A detailed table of the four endpoints (GET /devices, POST /devices/state, GET /climate/history, POST /security/arm) including their parameters and descriptions. 3) A troubleshooting section for the provided error codes. 4) A clear summary of rate limits.

API Specification:
{
  "base_url": "https://api.smarthome-nexus.io/v2.1",
  "auth": "Bearer Token in Header",
  "endpoints": [
    {"path": "/devices", "method": "GET", "desc": "Lists all connected IoT devices", "params": ["room_id", "type"]},
    {"path": "/devices/state", "method": "POST", "desc": "Updates device power/brightness", "body": {"device_id": "string", "action": "on|off", "value": "int"}},
    {"path": "/climate/history", "method": "GET", "desc": "Returns temperature and humidity logs for the last 24 hours", "params": ["sensor_id"]},
    {"path": "/security/arm", "method": "POST", "desc": "Arms or disarms the home security system", "body": {"mode": "stay|away", "pin": "int"}}
  ],
  "error_codes": {
    "401": "Unauthorized - Invalid or expired Token",
    "403": "Forbidden - User does not have permission for this device",
    "429": "Too Many Requests - Limit of 100 requests per minute exceeded",
    "503": "Service Unavailable - Communication timeout with the local hub"
  }
}

I need to create a technical documentation page for our internal 'Inventory Management API' (version 2.1.0). Based on the JSON schema provided below, please generate a structured documentation layout. Include: 1) A high-level summary of the API's purpose. 2) A detailed table for the 'POST /v2/items' endpoint covering all parameters, their types, and whether they are required. 3) A 'Response Codes' section explaining 200, 400, and 500 errors. 4) A Python code snippet using the 'requests' library to demonstrate a valid POST request.

Schema:
{
  "endpoint": "/v2/items",
  "method": "POST",
  "parameters": {
    "item_name": {"type": "string", "required": true, "description": "The unique name of the inventory item."},
    "sku": {"type": "string", "required": true, "description": "Stock Keeping Unit identifier."},
    "quantity": {"type": "integer", "required": true, "description": "Number of units to add."},
    "warehouse_id": {"type": "integer", "required": false, "default": 1, "description": "The ID of the storage facility."},
    "category": {"type": "string", "required": false, "enum": ["electronics", "furniture", "apparel"], "description": "Product category."}
  }
}

